WEBVTT

00:01.570 --> 00:04.590
Let's stay up all night chatting, young master.

00:04.590 --> 00:06.810
Tell us all about your youthful troubles.

00:07.330 --> 00:10.450
You're hoping I'll entertain you
while you drink, aren't you?

00:10.450 --> 00:13.310
Screw this. I'm going home. Let go.

00:13.310 --> 00:17.730
Oh, come on. Tell us everything
that's on your mind.

00:17.730 --> 00:20.700
We're such good friends, aren't we?

00:20.700 --> 00:22.090
Like hell we are. Let go.

00:27.370 --> 00:33.840
Snake

00:39.800 --> 00:42.390
What's wrong with you? Hit him back.

00:48.850 --> 00:50.590
All right! Right there.

00:50.590 --> 00:52.480
Seriously? Again?

00:58.970 --> 01:00.320
Those morons.

01:00.320 --> 01:02.110
They fell.

01:02.110 --> 01:04.070
Does that make it a tie?

01:06.580 --> 01:10.860
Nobody knows what they're talking about.

01:11.410 --> 01:14.210
They don't get it.

01:14.210 --> 01:17.420
They don't even know what they don't know.

01:17.970 --> 01:24.180
There's no way they can understand me
when they don't know what they don't know.

01:25.610 --> 01:28.450
Actually, I understand, young master.

01:28.450 --> 01:31.230
After all, 17 is a weird age.

01:31.230 --> 01:33.060
Not quite an adult, but no longer a kid.

01:35.940 --> 01:36.850
More.

01:36.850 --> 01:39.170
Sure thing.

01:39.170 --> 01:42.440
Here you go. Whoops.

01:45.190 --> 01:46.600
Look at you drink!

01:49.190 --> 01:56.120
Fox, Badger... You're actually laughing
at me on the inside, aren't you?

01:56.650 --> 01:58.890
He's not a fun drunk today.

01:58.890 --> 02:01.210
I'm starting to sober up.

02:01.210 --> 02:02.920
We shouldn't have invited him.

02:02.920 --> 02:05.050
I can hear you!

02:05.900 --> 02:11.310
You think bodyguards like you
have the right to mock me?

02:11.920 --> 02:14.690
You serve my dad for a pittance.

02:14.690 --> 02:17.020
Don't you have any pride as warriors?

02:17.590 --> 02:19.970
Please, call us guests.

02:19.970 --> 02:23.450
Even men like us are useful in a fight.

02:24.610 --> 02:26.240
Oh?

02:26.560 --> 02:28.650
You guys actually work sometimes?

02:28.650 --> 02:30.510
I've never seen you do your job, Fox.

02:30.510 --> 02:34.750
This village is so peaceful,
we're bored out of our minds.

02:35.380 --> 02:37.120
Draw your sword.

02:37.120 --> 02:39.560
I'll test your skills to make sure
you haven't lost your touch.

02:54.410 --> 02:55.310
See?

02:56.690 --> 03:00.980
We're your father's guests,
and this is what he pays us to do.

03:04.990 --> 03:08.300
Damn it! Just kill me!

03:10.730 --> 03:12.830
What should we do, Fox?

03:13.890 --> 03:15.810
That's odd.

03:15.810 --> 03:20.130
We were supposed to have fun drinking
together so Ketil's family would like us.

03:21.490 --> 03:24.130
I'm a nobody!

03:30.760 --> 03:33.200
In other words, young master,

03:33.200 --> 03:38.810
you don't like being treated
like a child by respectable folk.

03:38.810 --> 03:42.150
You guys treat me like one, too.

03:42.680 --> 03:45.100
What do you expect?

03:45.100 --> 03:47.610
You really are half a man.

03:47.610 --> 03:49.470
But for you to become a real man—

03:50.660 --> 03:52.850
Hey, you should be cheering him up.

03:52.850 --> 03:55.710
Quiet, you. I'm going somewhere with this.

03:55.710 --> 03:57.400
Just shut up and listen.

03:58.070 --> 03:59.870
You know, young master...

04:00.840 --> 04:05.760
Becoming a real man
isn't actually that difficult.

04:06.920 --> 04:11.630
All you gotta do is complete a...
rite of passage, I think it's called.

04:19.370 --> 04:21.740
You need to kill a person.

04:25.400 --> 04:31.160
Killing a person will make
you feel really confident.

04:32.180 --> 04:34.090
You oughta try it.

04:36.980 --> 04:43.210
Once you know how fragile human bodies are,
you won't be afraid of others anymore.

04:43.790 --> 04:45.850
It'll grow you right up.

04:46.930 --> 04:51.110
It's how all boys become men.

04:54.620 --> 04:57.850
B-But... who?

04:57.850 --> 05:01.260
Well, that's obvious.

05:01.260 --> 05:05.860
I know of the perfect target for a beginner.

05:10.650 --> 05:14.570
You've even got some right here on this farm.

05:22.420 --> 05:26.700
People you're allowed to kill.

07:13.350 --> 07:15.530
Boy, I slept well.

07:16.420 --> 07:17.990
I'm hungry.

07:18.570 --> 07:22.580
One, two, three, four.

07:23.120 --> 07:28.380
There's still a lot more wheat
to harvest today.

07:28.380 --> 07:32.590
This farm is way too big.

07:37.750 --> 07:42.110
At this rate, we'll have hardly any time
to clear the woods for next spring.

07:42.510 --> 07:46.140
I'd like to get it done in time
for the fall planting season.

07:47.140 --> 07:52.700
But first, we've gotta dig up the roots
and rocks, till the soil, and let it rest.

07:53.310 --> 07:55.820
I wonder if they'll let us
borrow a heavy plow.

08:05.650 --> 08:08.250
Th-Thorfinn, what's wrong?

08:08.810 --> 08:11.790
Are you still asleep? Hey, Thorfinn.

08:19.210 --> 08:21.290
Are you okay?

08:21.290 --> 08:23.510
You were screaming like crazy.

08:31.220 --> 08:34.470
What kind of dream
makes a man scream like that?

08:37.390 --> 08:38.520
I was dreaming?

08:39.370 --> 08:43.210
I wonder what it was. I can't remember.

08:49.860 --> 08:53.660
Go wash your face and let's get
started on our morning tasks.

08:57.100 --> 08:59.880
Dreams you forget are better left forgotten.

09:21.330 --> 09:24.530
Good morning. It's a nice morning, isn't it?

09:24.530 --> 09:27.160
Uh, yes. Good morning.

09:27.160 --> 09:28.810
Would you like to wash your faces?

09:28.810 --> 09:31.530
Go ahead. I'm already finished.

09:31.530 --> 09:33.020
Oh, no. I mean, yes.

09:33.020 --> 09:35.170
Uh, sorry. Take your time.

09:35.530 --> 09:39.790
Washing this face won't make it any better.

09:40.170 --> 09:42.310
Oh, I wouldn't say that.

09:43.250 --> 09:46.060
I think you have a wonderful face.

09:50.720 --> 09:53.410
Are you all right? Are you not feeling well?

09:53.410 --> 09:55.440
It's my heart...

09:55.440 --> 09:57.440
That's terrible. Does it hurt?

09:57.440 --> 10:01.070
No, I'm fine. I'm not sick or anything.

10:01.070 --> 10:02.430
Then are you injured?

10:02.430 --> 10:06.010
What is this? I feel so uneasy.

10:08.400 --> 10:14.760
I must have been dreaming
about something I mustn't forget.

10:18.840 --> 10:21.530
My name is Arnheid.

10:21.530 --> 10:23.610
You came here recently, didn't you?

10:23.610 --> 10:25.740
Y-Yes. I'm Einar.

10:25.740 --> 10:27.720
I'm from England.

10:28.000 --> 10:34.350
England? You speak the language so well,
I thought you were Norse.

10:34.350 --> 10:40.720
Everyone in my village, including me,
is descended from Nords.

10:40.720 --> 10:44.060
We all speak English and Norse.

10:44.060 --> 10:48.390
Though I'm sure it's hard for a lady like you
to understand me, since my accent is so thick.

10:50.040 --> 10:53.180
Oh, that's right. Excuse me.

10:53.180 --> 10:56.700
I hadn't mentioned
my status here on the farm.

11:02.660 --> 11:06.720
What? Aren't you the master's daughter?

11:06.720 --> 11:09.470
No, I'm not.

11:11.460 --> 11:14.330
Like you, I'm a slave.

11:14.860 --> 11:17.640
I'm the master's personal attendant.

11:18.610 --> 11:19.550
What?

11:25.740 --> 11:27.760
Good morning, gentlemen.

11:27.760 --> 11:31.820
Have you slaves gotten together
this morning to plot your escape?

11:32.160 --> 11:33.790
Good morning.

11:35.010 --> 11:36.750
You, what's your name?

11:37.290 --> 11:38.470
Thorfinn.

11:39.360 --> 11:42.750
Are you a slave, too? I don't recognize you.

11:42.750 --> 11:46.380
I'm E-Einar. I arrived this summer.

11:50.260 --> 11:56.790
Thorfinn and Einar, come with me.

12:07.960 --> 12:10.790
We're having a busy morning.

12:13.270 --> 12:16.290
Who are those guys?

12:16.610 --> 12:18.620
They've got swords.

12:19.600 --> 12:22.290
They aren't respectable folk, are they?

12:24.530 --> 12:25.970
They're "guests."

12:25.970 --> 12:29.180
They're the resident
defensive force at the farm.

12:30.310 --> 12:31.740
Basically bodyguards.

12:34.210 --> 12:39.750
Whatever business they've
got with us can't be good.

12:42.950 --> 12:45.720
I think you have a wonderful face.

12:48.820 --> 12:51.820
What is it? You're in a good mood, Einar.

12:51.820 --> 12:53.820
Oh, sorry.

12:54.140 --> 12:55.820
No problem at all.

12:55.820 --> 12:58.830
You seem like a lively one.

13:25.910 --> 13:27.650
Go on, young master.

13:27.650 --> 13:31.450
Make a nice clean cut.

13:32.310 --> 13:35.530
A clean cut? You mean...

13:35.530 --> 13:38.990
Very perceptive of you, big man.

13:38.990 --> 13:40.030
What?

13:40.980 --> 13:44.500
This ritual will allow the young master
to become a man.

13:45.570 --> 13:46.950
Die for us.

13:56.730 --> 14:00.280
This ritual will allow the young master
to become a man.

14:00.280 --> 14:01.690
Die for us.

14:06.810 --> 14:09.230
Y-You can't be serious!

14:09.230 --> 14:12.900
What have we done to deserve this?

14:12.900 --> 14:14.890
You've done nothing wrong!

14:14.890 --> 14:20.370
But your lives aren't your own.
That's all there is to it.

14:20.370 --> 14:24.970
Your rightful owner is free to do
whatever he pleases with his possessions.

14:24.970 --> 14:29.340
You're a slave that belongs to Olmar's family.

14:29.340 --> 14:33.340
He's going to cut you down himself.
You should be honored.

14:33.340 --> 14:34.970
Lucky you.

14:36.020 --> 14:37.580
Just give up already.

14:40.710 --> 14:44.890
Th-These guys belong to my dad.

14:44.890 --> 14:46.350
They're not mine.

14:46.880 --> 14:49.080
If I cut them down,
I'll have to pay him back for them.

14:51.110 --> 14:53.420
Pathetic, young master.

14:53.420 --> 14:55.860
You've made it this far,
and you're still making excuses?

14:56.610 --> 14:58.780
Are you afraid of your father?

14:58.780 --> 15:00.810
Are you afraid to kill?

15:00.810 --> 15:02.630
Or are you afraid of both?

15:02.630 --> 15:05.750
Shut up! I'm not scared of anything.

15:06.060 --> 15:09.630
Then do it. Make a nice clean cut.

15:11.750 --> 15:14.070
Thorfinn, run.

15:15.380 --> 15:16.880
It'll be fine.

15:20.600 --> 15:21.870
Damn you...

15:22.800 --> 15:25.330
What are you doing? Go, Thorfinn!

15:25.330 --> 15:26.950
Tell the master!

15:27.620 --> 15:29.450
You can do it, sir!

15:29.450 --> 15:31.310
Your opponent is raring to go!

15:34.560 --> 15:36.220
Don't move, shorty.

15:36.690 --> 15:38.430
Shut up and watch.

15:53.290 --> 15:54.790
What a pain.

15:57.880 --> 15:59.610
He can cut me down.

16:00.970 --> 16:02.410
You've got this, sir.

16:04.970 --> 16:07.420
You only need one of us, don't you?

16:08.350 --> 16:10.670
Let him return to work.

16:11.720 --> 16:13.420
He can cut me down.

16:51.510 --> 16:53.240
Ow...

16:57.010 --> 16:58.730
Oh, it's morning.

17:04.090 --> 17:06.220
Hey, Gramps.

17:07.250 --> 17:09.990
Gramps, are you there?

17:25.090 --> 17:29.070
Gramps, where's my breakfast?

17:29.070 --> 17:30.930
Gramps!

17:30.930 --> 17:34.770
You're asking about breakfast
after waking up at this hour?

17:34.770 --> 17:39.470
If you want to eat, help me with the
harvest every once in a while.

17:39.470 --> 17:41.570
No way.

17:41.570 --> 17:44.400
Then I'm not cooking for you.

17:44.400 --> 17:47.080
Figure something out yourself.

17:47.960 --> 17:49.420
That old fart.

17:49.420 --> 17:52.310
I'm not cooking for myself.
What a pain in the butt.

17:52.750 --> 17:55.100
I guess I'll head home.

18:11.320 --> 18:13.850
I'll allow Master Olmar to cut me down.

18:14.390 --> 18:17.100
Please let Einar return to work.

18:18.050 --> 18:19.800
We have another busy day.

18:23.500 --> 18:25.050
Wh-What did you just say?

18:37.130 --> 18:40.670
Sorry, what's your name again?

18:41.770 --> 18:43.000
It's Thorfinn.

18:43.820 --> 18:45.980
All right, Thorfinn.

18:45.980 --> 18:49.840
Do you understand what you just said?

18:49.840 --> 18:52.890
Being cut down means dying.

18:54.310 --> 18:55.670
Yes, it certainly does.

18:58.230 --> 19:01.480
You idiot! What are you—

19:03.170 --> 19:06.620
Keep your mouth shut. Stay out of this.

19:07.700 --> 19:09.900
Did you hear that, boys?

19:09.900 --> 19:13.510
You run into guys like him
every once in a while.

19:15.060 --> 19:20.430
I can't overlook what you just said.

19:20.430 --> 19:26.130
Letting a remark like that slide
reduces the value of our product.

19:27.300 --> 19:33.820
Hey, Thorfinn. Do you know
what product we warriors sell?

19:36.020 --> 19:37.030
No.

19:40.250 --> 19:41.480
It's death.

19:49.240 --> 19:52.240
Everyone is afraid to die.

19:52.240 --> 19:55.260
I can tell you for certain
that everyone fears it.

19:55.890 --> 19:57.790
Look at the young master.

19:57.790 --> 19:59.930
He's even afraid of someone else dying.

19:59.930 --> 20:02.380
Shut up. I'm not s-scared.

20:02.830 --> 20:07.630
You should be.
Death has value because we fear it.

20:08.040 --> 20:12.140
Otherwise we wouldn't be able
to use our swords to make a living.

20:21.970 --> 20:24.280
You should be scared, too.

20:25.060 --> 20:26.590
Go on. Be afraid.

20:32.090 --> 20:34.540
Aw, man. I'm hungry.

20:35.320 --> 20:37.620
Hey, you punks.

20:40.570 --> 20:42.350
Stop!

20:44.810 --> 20:49.100
Those idiots. They're up to no good again.

20:50.130 --> 20:51.830
Stop!

20:52.640 --> 20:55.890
Damn it! You monsters!

20:57.650 --> 20:58.670
Come on.

20:59.140 --> 21:01.230
Beg for your life.

21:01.710 --> 21:04.970
Don't hide your true feelings, Thorfinn.

21:11.050 --> 21:12.300
Ouch.

21:12.700 --> 21:19.950
If you don't hurry up, your tiny
little body will end up even smaller.

21:27.210 --> 21:33.090
Huh, he didn't even blink. Impressive.

21:34.210 --> 21:37.980
Isn't that one of the master's slaves?

21:43.560 --> 21:48.870
Why do we have to fear death?

21:53.510 --> 21:56.090
Do we live because we don't want to die?

21:59.110 --> 22:04.140
Does anything good come from being alive?

22:10.440 --> 22:12.040
Not for me.

22:16.950 --> 22:23.020
Not a single good thing has
happened to me in my entire life.

22:44.470 --> 22:46.070
Your eye is next.

22:49.700 --> 22:50.860
Show me that you're afraid.

22:51.300 --> 22:52.460
Don't, Fox!

22:58.840 --> 23:00.540
S-Snake...

23:10.480 --> 23:14.060
Aw, man. He's in rough shape.

23:17.530 --> 23:22.810
B-Boss, welcome back.
Wh-Wh-When did you get here?

23:22.810 --> 23:23.620
Fox.

23:23.620 --> 23:24.730
Yes, sir.

23:26.250 --> 23:27.250
Come closer.

23:27.250 --> 23:28.570
Y-Yes, sir.

23:45.290 --> 23:46.290
Badger.

23:46.290 --> 23:47.690
Yes, sir!

23:52.450 --> 23:53.750
Explain.

25:36.670 --> 25:39.760
Awakening

25:37.800 --> 25:39.070
"Awakening."
